(ns kotoba.compiler.affine
  "Is this vector binding used LINEARLY — read any number of times, then
  consumed at most once, and never mentioned again, on every path?

  ## Why the question is worth asking

  `vector-assoc` allocates. The native host says so in its own words: *every
  operation that changes an element allocates rather than mutates*, and
  `checked_vector_assoc` is a `memmove` of the whole vector followed by a bump
  into an arena that is never reclaimed. Two consequences, both measured
  rather than reasoned about:

  - one element write costs O(length)
  - the number of writes a vector may ever receive is
    `arena / length` — **a 16,384-item vector, the longest KIR admits, can be
    updated four times in the life of a program** (65,536 / 16,384)

  An order book is a struct of arrays with about a million slots per field and
  a write on every order. Both numbers are wrong for it by orders of
  magnitude, and neither is a safety property: `surface-status.edn` classifies
  the whole native vector entry `:implemented-partial`, and its `:state` entry
  says plainly that **the invariant is AMBIENT, not mutation itself**.

  ## What linearity buys, and why it is not a new semantics

  If a vector handle is dead after an update, updating it in place and
  allocating a copy are indistinguishable to every observer. So this analysis
  does not change what a program MEANS. It decides when the backend may lower
  `vector-assoc` to a store instead of a copy, which is why the answer has to
  be conservative: a wrong `true` here silently mutates a value somebody still
  holds.

  ## What conservative means here

  `false` for anything not obviously linear. The shapes admitted are the ones
  a struct-of-arrays actually writes:

      (let [v (vector-i64-new n)
            v (vector-assoc v 0 x)      ; shadows — the old v is dead
            v (vector-assoc v 1 y)]
        (vector-at v 0))

  ## The question is ORDER, not count

  What makes an in-place store observable is a read that runs AFTER it
  through a name that still means the old value. A read that runs BEFORE the
  store returns a scalar (`vector-at` of a vector-i64 is an i64) and holds
  nothing afterwards, so any number of them are indistinguishable from the
  copy. So the analysis walks each path in EVALUATION order with three
  states -- live, spent, refused -- rather than counting occurrences:

  - reads while live: admitted, any number of them, at any index
  - one consuming use (an update, a proved linear-returning call, or -- where
    the caller opted in -- the return): live -> spent
  - anything after spent that mentions the handle: refused
  - the handle anywhere that is not a vector operation: refused (an escape)

  This admits what a struct of arrays has to do -- read several fields, then
  write -- which the count could not: `(let [h (vector-at v k) ...]
  (vector-assoc! v j h))` is two occurrences and one path, and was refused
  for a reason that was never about safety. It is also what made the fused
  `v[k] += delta` (superproject ADR-2609010500) need its own rule; under
  order it is simply a read inside the update's own arguments, which are
  evaluated before the update runs.

  Evaluation order is only ASSUMED where the language fixes it: `let`
  initialisers and bodies, `do`, the bodies of `when`/`when-not`/`when-let`
  (sequences, not alternatives -- counting them as alternatives admitted a
  read after a store, measured below), a test before its arms. The arguments
  of an ordinary call have no order this analysis relies on: when more than
  one of them mentions the handle they must all be pure reads. A body that
  runs later than it is written (`fn`, `delay`, ...) may not mention the
  handle at all, and one that runs repeatedly (`loop`, `dotimes`, ...) may
  only read it.

  Measured 2026-09-23 before this rewrite, amu 34bba745 aarch64-macos under
  kexe_loader: `(when (= c 1) (vector-assoc! v 0 5) (vector-at v 0))` was
  ADMITTED and answered 5; the same program as `(if (= c 1) (do ...) 0)` was
  refused, and with the copying `vector-assoc` it answered 0. `when` was in
  the set of branching heads, so its two body forms were counted as two
  alternatives and the maximum was 1.

  Escape analysis for literals already exists next door in
  `kotoba.native.vector-region`; this is the same posture applied to the
  update path rather than to construction.

  ## Why it lives in the frontend

  It first landed in `kotoba-native`, next to `kotoba.native.vector-region`,
  which is a similar-looking escape analysis. Wrong home: this reads SOURCE,
  `kotoba-sema` is what holds source, and a backend repo is not on this one's
  dependency path -- so the gate could never have been consulted from where
  the decision is made."
  {:kotoba/export [*linear-returning* consuming expand-threads in-place-candidates linear-let-thread? linear-parameter? linear-returning? linear? module-linear-returning producing reading unanalysable-thread]}
  (:require 
            [kotoba.form :as form])
  (:schemas {:form/r [:record :form/r [[:tag :i64] [:s :string] [:n :i64] [:k :keyword]
                                          [:kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:span :i64] [:data :bytes]]]
                                 :form/rd [:record :form/rd [[:form [:ref :form/r]] [:pos :i64]]]}))

;; clojure.core/some, spelled as the loop it is. In Kotoba `some` is the
;; option constructor and a two-argument `(some pred coll)` is refused as a
;; name collision (kotoba-sema frontend); this is the same definition as
;; clojure.core/some -- the first logical-true (pred x), in order, stopping
;; there -- so the host answer is unchanged on nbb and the JVM.
(defn- fget [m [:ref :form/r] k :keyword] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [kids (form/kids-of m) n (vector-count kids)]
       (loop [j 0]
         (if (>= (+ j 1) n)
           (form/nil-form)
           (let [x (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids j)]
             (if (and (form/is-keyword? x) (= (form/keyword-value x) k))
               (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids (+ j 1))
               (recur (+ j 2))))))))

(defn- member? [x [:ref :form/r] xs [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (form/count-of xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false (if (form/eq (form/nth-of xs i) x) true (recur (inc i)))))))

(defn- sym-in? [f [:ref :form/r] text :string] :bool
     (and (form/is-symbol? f) (member? f (form/edn-form text))))

(defn- sym-is? [f [:ref :form/r] name :string] :bool
     (and (form/is-symbol? f) (string=? (form/symbol-value f) name)))

(defn- num [n :i64] [:ref :form/r] (form/int-form n))

(defn- drop-list [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] from :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i from acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n) acc (recur (inc i) (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)))))))

(defn- take-list [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] upto :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (or (>= i n) (>= i upto)) acc (recur (inc i) (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)))))))

(defn- every-nth [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] from :i64 step :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i from acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n) acc (recur (+ i step) (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)))))))



(defn consuming
     "Operations that make the vector they are given dead."
     [] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/edn-form "#{vector-assoc vector-f64-assoc vector-conj vector-f64-conj vector-drop vector-f64-drop vector-assoc! vector-f64-assoc!}"))

(defn- consuming-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "vector-assoc") (string=? sn "vector-f64-assoc") (string=? sn "vector-conj") (string=? sn "vector-f64-conj") (string=? sn "vector-drop") (string=? sn "vector-f64-drop") (string=? sn "vector-assoc!") (string=? sn "vector-f64-assoc!"))))))



(defn producing
     "Heads that hand back a vector this binding OWNS."
     [] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/edn-form "#{vector-alloc vector-new vector-assoc vector-assoc! vector-conj vector-drop vector-f64-alloc vector-f64-new vector-f64-assoc vector-f64-assoc! vector-f64-conj vector-f64-drop}"))

(defn- producing-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "vector-alloc") (string=? sn "vector-new") (string=? sn "vector-assoc") (string=? sn "vector-assoc!") (string=? sn "vector-conj") (string=? sn "vector-drop") (string=? sn "vector-f64-alloc") (string=? sn "vector-f64-new") (string=? sn "vector-f64-assoc") (string=? sn "vector-f64-assoc!") (string=? sn "vector-f64-conj") (string=? sn "vector-f64-drop"))))))



(defn reading
     "Operations that observe without consuming."
     [] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/edn-form "#{vector-count vector-f64-count vector-at vector-f64-at vector-get vector-f64-get nth bytes-from-vector-i64}"))

(defn- reading-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "vector-count") (string=? sn "vector-f64-count") (string=? sn "vector-at") (string=? sn "vector-f64-at") (string=? sn "vector-get") (string=? sn "vector-f64-get") (string=? sn "nth") (string=? sn "bytes-from-vector-i64"))))))




(defn- let-form? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (form/is-seq? f) (sym-is? (form/first-of f) "let") (form/is-vec? (form/nth-of f 1))))





(defn *linear-returning*
     "The `[name parameter-index]` pairs this module has proved LINEAR-RETURNING.
     Empty by default. Kotoba has no dynamic binding, so the analysis threads the
     set as an explicit argument (the extra arity of each export)."
     [] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-vec (form/no-forms)))

(defn- pair-hit? [pair [:ref :form/r] f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     ;; PAIR = [name index]; does F call NAME with TARGET at that parameter slot?
     (and (form/eq (form/nth-of pair 0) (form/first-of f))
          (form/eq target (form/nth-of f (inc (form/int-value (form/nth-of pair 1)))))))

(defn- lr-call? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (form/is-seq? f) (form/is-symbol? (form/first-of f))
          (let [n (form/count-of lr)]
            (loop [i 0]
              (if (>= i n) false (if (pair-hit? (form/nth-of lr i) f target) true (recur (inc i))))))))

(defn- lr-position [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [n (form/count-of lr)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) 0
           (let [pair (form/nth-of lr i)]
             (if (pair-hit? pair f target) (inc (form/int-value (form/nth-of pair 1))) (recur (inc i))))))))



(defn- linear-returning-call? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool (lr-call? f target lr))



(defn- consuming-call? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (form/is-seq? f)
          (or (and (consuming-head? (form/first-of f)) (form/eq target (form/nth-of f 1)))
              (linear-returning-call? f target lr))))



(defn- reading-call? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (form/is-seq? f) (reading-head? (form/first-of f)) (form/eq target (form/nth-of f 1))))



;; ── threading, before anything is counted ───────────────────────────────────
;;
;; The frontend desugars `->` into nested calls, but this analysis reads
;; SOURCE, so it used to see `(-> v (vector-assoc! 0 5))` as a call to `->`
;; with `v` in it and `(vector-assoc! 0 5)` as a write whose handle is the
;; literal 0. The real handle was never checked. Measured 2026-09-23 on amu
;; with kotoba-sema 3fdaefb6, aarch64-macos under kexe_loader:
;;
;;     (let [w (-> v (vector-assoc! 0 5))] (+ (vector-at w 0) (vector-at v 0)))
;;
;; was admitted and answered 10; with `vector-assoc` it answers 5. And a local
;; that happened to sit in the index position of a threaded step was taken
;; for a handle and refused for being read elsewhere. So the thread is
;; expanded first -- the same rewrite the frontend's `thread-form` makes.

(defn- in-place-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "vector-assoc!") (string=? sn "vector-f64-assoc!"))))))



(defn- unexpanded-thread? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "cond->") (string=? sn "cond->>") (string=? sn "some->") (string=? sn "some->>") (string=? sn "doto"))))))



(defn- thread-step [value [:ref :form/r] step [:ref :form/r] last? :bool] [:ref :form/r]
     (cond
       (form/is-symbol? step) (form/call1 (form/symbol-value step) value)
       (and (form/is-seq? step) (> (form/count-of step) 0))
       (if last?
         (form/form-seq (form/append-form (form/kids-of step) value))
         (form/form-seq (form/cons-onto (form/first-of step) (form/cons-onto value (form/rest-list step)))))
       :else (form/call2 "->" value step)))



(defn- any-thread? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false (if (contains-thread? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)) true (recur (inc i)))))))

(defn- contains-thread? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (cond
       (form/is-seq? f) (or (let [sx (form/first-of f)] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "->") (string=? sn "->>") (string=? sn "as->"))))) (any-thread? (form/kids-of f)))
       (or (form/is-map? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f)) (any-thread? (form/kids-of f))
       :else false))



(defn- expand-each [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n) acc (recur (inc i) (form/append-form acc (expand-threads (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i))))))))

(defn- fold-thread [initial [:ref :form/r] steps [:list [:ref :form/r]] last? :bool] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count steps)]
       (loop [i 0 value initial]
         (if (>= i n) value (recur (inc i) (thread-step value (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] steps i) last?))))))

(defn- fold-as [initial [:ref :form/r] name [:ref :form/r] steps [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count steps)]
       (loop [i 0 value initial]
         (if (>= i n)
           value
           (recur (inc i) (form/call2 "let" (form/vec2 name value) (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] steps i)))))))

(defn expand-threads
     "`form` with every `->`, `->>` and `as->` rewritten to what it means."
     [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (cond
       (not (contains-thread? f)) f
       (and (form/is-seq? f) (let [sx (form/first-of f)] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "->") (string=? sn "->>"))))) (> (form/count-of f) 1))
       (expand-threads (fold-thread (form/nth-of f 1) (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2) (sym-is? (form/first-of f) "->>")))
       (and (form/is-seq? f) (sym-is? (form/first-of f) "as->") (<= 3 (form/count-of f)) (form/is-symbol? (form/nth-of f 2)))
       (expand-threads (fold-as (form/nth-of f 1) (form/nth-of f 2) (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 3)))
       (form/is-seq? f) (form/form-seq (expand-each (form/kids-of f)))
       (form/is-vec? f) (form/form-vec (expand-each (form/kids-of f)))
       (form/is-map? f) (form/form-map (expand-each (form/kids-of f)))
       (form/is-set? f) (form/form-set (expand-each (form/kids-of f)))
       :else f))



(defn- any-in-place? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false (if (contains-in-place? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)) true (recur (inc i)))))))

(defn- contains-in-place? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (cond
       (form/is-seq? f) (or (in-place-head? (form/first-of f)) (any-in-place? (form/kids-of f)))
       (or (form/is-map? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f)) (any-in-place? (form/kids-of f))
       :else false))



(defn- first-unanalysable [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form/nil-form)
           (let [r (unanalysable-thread (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i))]
             (if (not (form/is-nil? r)) r (recur (inc i))))))))

(defn unanalysable-thread
     "The first `cond->`-style form in `form` that writes in place, or nil."
     [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (cond
       (and (form/is-seq? f) (unexpanded-thread? (form/first-of f)) (contains-in-place? f)) f
       (or (form/is-map? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f) (form/is-seq? f)) (first-unanalysable (form/kids-of f))
       :else (form/nil-form)))



;; ── the walk, in evaluation order ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;
;; States: `:live` (only read so far), `:spent` (consumed, or handed back in
;; tail position), `::refused`. A state only moves forward. See the ns
;; docstring for why this replaced a use COUNT.

(defn- deferred-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "fn") (string=? sn "fn*") (string=? sn "letfn") (string=? sn "delay") (string=? sn "lazy-seq") (string=? sn "for") (string=? sn "reify"))))))



(defn- repeating-head? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (let [sx f] (and (form/is-symbol? sx) (let [sn (form/symbol-value sx)] (or (string=? sn "loop") (string=? sn "doseq") (string=? sn "dotimes") (string=? sn "while"))))))



(defn- occurs-any? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false (if (occurs? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) target) true (recur (inc i)))))))

(defn- occurs? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (cond
       (form/eq f target) true
       (or (form/is-seq? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f) (form/is-map? f)) (occurs-any? (form/kids-of f) target)
       :else false))



(defn- max2 [a :i64 b :i64] :i64 (if (> a b) a b))



(defn- pair-inits [bindings [:ref :form/r] from :i64 upto :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (loop [p from acc (form/no-forms)]
       (if (>= p upto) acc (recur (inc p) (form/append-form acc (form/nth-of bindings (+ (* 2 p) 1)))))))

(defn- pair-count [bindings [:ref :form/r]] :i64 (quot (form/count-of bindings) 2))



(defn- walk-seq [forms [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [n (vector-count forms)]
       (loop [i 0 s state]
         (if (>= i n)
           s
           (if (= s 2)
             s
             (recur (inc i) (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] forms i) target (and tail? (= i (dec n))) s lr)))))))



(defn- touching [args [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count args)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n) acc
           (let [a (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] args i)]
             (recur (inc i) (if (occurs? a target) (form/append-form acc a) acc)))))))

(defn- all-unchanged? [ts [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r] state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count ts)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true
           (if (= state (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] ts i) target false state lr)) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn- walk-unordered [args [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r] state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [ts (touching args target)
           c (vector-count ts)]
       (cond (= c 0) state
             (= c 1) (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] ts 0) target false state lr)
             :else (if (all-unchanged? ts target state lr) state 2))))



(defn- handle-position [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (if (and (consuming-head? (form/first-of f)) (form/eq target (form/nth-of f 1)))
       1
       (lr-position f target lr)))



(defn- without-index [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] i :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [k 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= k n) acc (recur (inc k) (if (= k i) acc (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs k))))))))



(defn- first-binding-index [bindings [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [np (pair-count bindings)]
       (loop [p 0]
         (if (>= p np) -1 (if (form/eq target (form/nth-of bindings (* 2 p))) p (recur (inc p)))))))

(defn- walk-let [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [bindings (form/nth-of f 1)
           np (pair-count bindings)
           i (first-binding-index bindings target)
           body (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2)]
       (if (< i 0)
         (walk-seq body target tail? (walk-seq (pair-inits bindings 0 np) target false state lr) lr)
         (if (occurs-any? (pair-inits bindings 0 (inc i)) target)
           2
           (walk-seq body target tail? (walk-seq (pair-inits bindings (inc i) np) target false 0 lr) lr)))))

(defn- join-arms [arms [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool s :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [n (vector-count arms)]
       (loop [i 0 m (if (< n 2) s 0)]
         (if (>= i n) m (recur (inc i) (max2 m (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] arms i) target tail? s lr)))))))

(defn- pairs-part [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] np :i64 offset :i64] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (loop [k 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
       (if (>= k np) acc (recur (inc k) (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs (+ (* 2 k) offset)))))))

(defn- walk-cond [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [clauses (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 1)
           np (quot (vector-count clauses) 2)
           tests (pairs-part clauses np 0)
           s (walk-seq tests target false state lr)]
       (loop [k 0 m s]
         (if (>= k np) m (recur (inc k) (max2 m (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] clauses (+ (* 2 k) 1)) target tail? s lr)))))))

(defn- walk-case [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [s (walk (form/nth-of f 1) target false state lr)
           clauses (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2)
           cn (vector-count clauses)
           np (quot cn 2)
           keys* (pairs-part clauses np 0)
           arms0 (pairs-part clauses np 1)
           arms (if (= 1 (- cn (* 2 np))) (form/append-form arms0 (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] clauses (dec cn))) arms0)]
       (if (occurs-any? keys* target)
         2
         (loop [k 0 m s]
           (if (>= k (vector-count arms)) m (recur (inc k) (max2 m (walk (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] arms k) target tail? s lr))))))))

(defn- walk-if-let [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [bindings (form/nth-of f 1)
           more (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2)
           s (if (form/is-vec? bindings)
               (if (occurs-any? (every-nth (form/kids-of bindings) 0 2) target)
                 (if (form/eq target (form/nth-of bindings 0)) 2 (walk-seq (every-nth (form/kids-of bindings) 1 2) target false state lr))
                 (walk-seq (every-nth (form/kids-of bindings) 1 2) target false state lr))
               2)]
       s))

(defn- walk-loop [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [bindings (form/nth-of f 1)
           np (pair-count bindings)
           i (first-binding-index bindings target)
           init (form/nth-of bindings (+ (* 2 i) 1))]
       (cond
         (occurs-any? (pair-inits bindings 0 np) target) 2
         (not (and (form/is-seq? init) (producing-head? (form/first-of init)))) 2
         (= 2 (walk-seq (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2) target false 0 lr)) 2
         :else state)))

(defn- names-include? [bindings [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (form/count-of bindings)]
       (loop [j 0]
         (if (>= j n) false (if (form/eq target (form/nth-of bindings j)) true (recur (+ j 2)))))))

(defn- walk [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool state :i64 lr [:ref :form/r]] :i64
     (let [head (form/first-of f)
           hp (if (form/is-seq? f) (handle-position f target lr) 0)]
       (cond
         (= state 2) state
         (not (occurs? f target)) state
         (form/eq f target) (if (and tail? (= state 0)) 1 2)
         (not (form/is-seq? f)) (walk-unordered (form/kids-of f) target state lr)
         (let-form? f) (walk-let f target tail? state lr)
         (sym-is? head "do") (walk-seq (form/rest-list f) target tail? state lr)
         (or (sym-is? head "if") (sym-is? head "if-not"))
         (let [s (walk (form/nth-of f 1) target false state lr)]
           (join-arms (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2) target tail? s lr))
         (or (sym-is? head "when") (sym-is? head "when-not"))
         (let [s (walk (form/nth-of f 1) target false state lr)]
           (max2 s (walk-seq (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2) target tail? s lr)))
         (or (sym-is? head "if-let") (sym-is? head "when-let"))
         (let [s (walk-if-let f target tail? state lr)
               more (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2)]
           (if (sym-is? head "if-let")
             (join-arms more target tail? s lr)
             (max2 s (walk-seq more target tail? s lr))))
         (sym-is? head "cond") (walk-cond f target tail? state lr)
         (sym-is? head "case") (walk-case f target tail? state lr)
         (deferred-head? head) 2
         (and (sym-is? head "loop") (form/is-vec? (form/nth-of f 1)) (names-include? (form/nth-of f 1) target))
         (walk-loop f target state lr)
         (repeating-head? head)
         (let [s (walk-seq (form/rest-list f) target false state lr)] (if (= s state) state 2))
         (> hp 0)
         (let [s (walk-unordered (without-index (form/kids-of f) hp) target state lr)] (if (= s 0) 1 2))
         (reading-call? f target)
         (let [s (walk-unordered (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2) target state lr)] (if (= s 0) 0 2))
         :else (walk-unordered (form/kids-of f) target state lr))))



(defn- ordered-ok? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] tail? :bool lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (not (= 2 (walk f target tail? 0 lr))))



;; The two walks below were a named `(fn walk ...)` closing over an atom. They
;; are plain recursive defns now: a fn value cannot be named or `swap!` an atom
;; (kotoba-sema frontend), and this module is on the compiler's own selfhost
;; path (superproject adr-2609242330). Same visit order (a let's own pairs, then
;; its children, maps as their flattened entries), same collected values.

(defn- let-children [f [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form/kids-of f))



(defn- let-inits-ok? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (if (let-form? f)
       (let [b (form/nth-of f 1)
             np (pair-count b)]
         (loop [p 0]
           (if (>= p np) true
             (let [init (form/nth-of b (+ (* 2 p) 1))]
               (if (or (not (form/eq target (form/nth-of b (* 2 p))))
                       (and (form/is-seq? init) (producing-head? (form/first-of init))))
                 (recur (inc p))
                 false)))))
       true))

(defn- children-owned? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true (if (inits-owned? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) target) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn- inits-owned? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (let-inits-ok? f target)
          (or (not (or (form/is-seq? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f) (form/is-map? f)))
              (children-owned? (form/kids-of f) target))))



(defn- names-here [f [:ref :form/r] acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (if (let-form? f)
       (let [b (form/nth-of f 1)
             np (pair-count b)]
         (loop [p 0 out acc]
           (if (>= p np) out
             (let [init (form/nth-of b (+ (* 2 p) 1))]
               (recur (inc p) (if (and (form/is-seq? init) (producing-head? (form/first-of init)))
                                (form/append-form out (form/nth-of b (* 2 p)))
                                out))))))
       acc))

(defn- producing-names [f [:ref :form/r] acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [here (names-here f acc)]
       (if (or (form/is-seq? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f) (form/is-map? f))
         (let [xs (form/kids-of f) n (vector-count xs)]
           (loop [i 0 out here]
             (if (>= i n) out (recur (inc i) (producing-names (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) out)))))
         here)))



(defn- owned-binding? [f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool (inits-owned? f target))



(defn linear-returning?
     "True when `target` is linear in `form` EXCEPT that `form` hands it back."
     ([f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool (linear-returning? f target (form/form-vec (form/no-forms))))
     ([f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
      (and (ordered-ok? f target true lr) (owned-binding? f target))))



(defn linear?
     "True when `target` may be updated in place inside `form`."
     ([f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r]] :bool (linear? f target (form/form-vec (form/no-forms))))
     ([f [:ref :form/r] target [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
      (and (ordered-ok? f target false lr) (owned-binding? f target))))



(defn- unused-binding-pairs [bindings [:ref :form/r]] :i64 (pair-count bindings))



(defn linear-parameter?
     "True when a function parameter is threaded linearly through its body."
     ([body [:ref :form/r] param [:ref :form/r]] :bool (linear? body param))
     ([body [:ref :form/r] param [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool (linear? body param lr)))



(defn- do-form-of [later [:list [:ref :form/r]] body [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-seq (form/cons-onto (form/symbol-form "do") (form/append-many later body))))

(defn- names-bound? [names [:ref :form/r] bindings [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (form/count-of names)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true
           (if (member? (form/nth-of names i) (every-nth-form bindings 0)) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn- every-nth-form [bindings [:ref :form/r] from :i64] [:ref :form/r]
     (form/form-vec (every-nth (form/kids-of bindings) from 2)))

(defn- later-inits [bindings [:ref :form/r] n [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [np (pair-count bindings)
           i (first-binding-index bindings n)]
       (if (< i 0) (form/no-forms) (pair-inits bindings (inc i) np))))

(defn- some-init-consumes? [bindings [:ref :form/r] n [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [np (pair-count bindings)]
       (loop [p 0]
         (if (>= p np) false
           (if (consuming-call? (form/nth-of bindings (+ (* 2 p) 1)) n lr) true (recur (inc p)))))))

(defn- thread-ordered? [names [:ref :form/r] bindings [:ref :form/r] body [:list [:ref :form/r]] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [c (form/count-of names)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i c) true
           (let [n (form/nth-of names i)]
             (if (ordered-ok? (do-form-of (later-inits bindings n) body) n false lr) (recur (inc i)) false))))))

(defn- thread-consumed? [names [:ref :form/r] bindings [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [c (dec (form/count-of names))]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i c) true (if (some-init-consumes? bindings (form/nth-of names i) lr) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn- body-linear? [body [:list [:ref :form/r]] live [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count body)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true (if (linear? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] body i) live lr) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn linear-let-thread?
     "True when a `let` threads a vector through DISTINCT names, each consuming
     the one before."
     ([f [:ref :form/r] names [:ref :form/r]] :bool (linear-let-thread? f names (form/form-vec (form/no-forms))))
     ([f [:ref :form/r] names [:ref :form/r] lr [:ref :form/r]] :bool
      (and (let-form? f) (<= 2 (form/count-of names))
           (let [bindings (form/nth-of f 1)
                 body (drop-list (form/kids-of f) 2)]
             (and (names-bound? names bindings)
                  (thread-ordered? names bindings body lr)
                  (thread-consumed? names bindings lr)
                  (body-linear? body (form/last-of names) lr))))))



;; --- the module half ---------------------------------------------------------

(defn- calls-into [f [:ref :form/r] name [:ref :form/r] acc [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [here (if (and (form/is-seq? f) (form/eq name (form/first-of f))) (form/append-form acc f) acc)]
       (if (or (form/is-seq? f) (form/is-vec? f) (form/is-set? f) (form/is-map? f))
         (let [xs (form/kids-of f) n (vector-count xs)]
           (loop [i 0 out here]
             (if (>= i n) out (recur (inc i) (calls-into (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) name out)))))
         here)))



(defn in-place-candidates
     "Names a `let` in `form` binds from a `producing` head."
     [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [names (producing-names f (form/no-forms))
           n (vector-count names)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form/form-set acc)
           (recur (inc i) (if (member? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] names i) (form/form-vec acc)) acc (form/append-form acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] names i))))))))



(defn- param-index-assumed? [params [:ref :form/r] caller [:ref :form/r] argument [:ref :form/r] assumed [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (form/count-of params)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false
           (if (and (form/eq argument (form/nth-of params i))
                    (member? (form/vec2 caller (form/int-form i)) assumed))
             true
             (recur (inc i)))))))

(defn- call-ok? [call [:ref :form/r] index :i64 whole [:ref :form/r] params [:ref :form/r] body [:ref :form/r] caller [:ref :form/r] assumed [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [argument (form/nth-of call (inc index))]
       (cond
         (> (inc index) (dec (form/count-of call))) false
         (not (form/is-symbol? argument)) true
         (not (or (member? argument params) (member? argument (in-place-candidates body)))) false
         :else (or (linear? whole argument assumed)
                   (and (linear-returning? whole argument assumed)
                        (param-index-assumed? params caller argument assumed))))))

(defn- function-gives-up? [function [:ref :form/r] name [:ref :form/r] index :i64 assumed [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [caller (form/nth-of function 0)
           params (form/nth-of function 1)
           body (form/nth-of function 2)
           whole (form/nth-of function 3)
           calls (calls-into whole name (form/no-forms))
           n (vector-count calls)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true
           (if (call-ok? (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] calls i) index whole params body caller assumed) (recur (inc i)) false)))))

(defn- caller-gives-it-up? [functions [:ref :form/r] name [:ref :form/r] index :i64 assumed [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (form/count-of functions)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) true
           (if (function-gives-up? (form/nth-of functions i) name index assumed) (recur (inc i)) false)))))



(defn- initial-pairs [functions [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (form/count-of functions)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form/form-set acc)
           (let [f (form/nth-of functions i)
                 pc (form/count-of (fget f :params))]
             (recur (inc i)
                    (loop [k 0 out acc]
                      (if (>= k pc) out (recur (inc k) (let [p (form/vec2 (fget f :name) (form/int-form k))] (if (member? p (form/form-vec out)) out (form/append-form out p))))))))))))

(defn- function-named [functions [:ref :form/r] name [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (form/count-of functions)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) (form/nil-form)
           (if (form/eq (form/nth-of (form/nth-of functions i) 0) name) (form/nth-of functions i) (recur (inc i)))))))

;; Each function once as the vector [name params body whole], whole = (do body...) (agent ARENA 2026-10-04): the
;; fixpoint below asks about every [name index] pair against every function, and rebuilding these per question was
;; the largest cost of a native analyze of compiler-sized modules (measured, docs/selfhost-arena-20261004.md).
(defn- prepare-functions [functions [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (form/count-of functions)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form/form-vec acc)
           (let [f (form/nth-of functions i)
                 body (fget f :body)]
             (recur (inc i)
                    (form/append-form acc (form/form-vec
                                           (form/append-form
                                            (form/three-forms (fget f :name) (fget f :params) body)
                                            (form/form-seq (form/cons-onto (form/symbol-form "do") (form/kids-of body))))))))))))

(defn- pair-survives? [pair [:ref :form/r] functions [:ref :form/r] assumed [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [name (form/nth-of pair 0)
           index (form/int-value (form/nth-of pair 1))
           f (function-named functions name)
           params (form/nth-of f 1)
           target (form/nth-of params index)]
       (and (< index (form/count-of params))
            (form/is-symbol? target)
            (linear-returning? (form/nth-of f 3) target assumed)
            (caller-gives-it-up? functions name index assumed))))

(defn- surviving-pairs [functions [:ref :form/r] assumed [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (form/count-of assumed)]
       (loop [i 0 out (form/no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form/form-set out)
           (let [p (form/nth-of assumed i)]
             (recur (inc i) (if (pair-survives? p functions assumed) (form/append-form out p) out)))))))

(defn module-linear-returning
     "The `[name parameter-index]` pairs a module may treat as linear-returning:
     a greatest fixpoint, shrinking from every parameter of every function."
     [functions [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [prepared (prepare-functions functions)]
       (loop [assumed (initial-pairs functions)]
         (let [surviving (surviving-pairs prepared assumed)]
           (if (form/eq surviving assumed) assumed (recur surviving))))))
